   151	sets that we mine from 10 large open-source projects, spanning 28
   152	development years, to address the following research questions:
   153	**RQ1. Impact Prevalence:** _**How often do build-modifying change**_
   154	_**sets propagate their impact beyond the local scope?**_
   155	_Motivation:_ The usefulness of BCIA will depend on how often the
   156	impact of the changes propagates in non-obvious ways. If changes
   157	frequently propagate an impact, then the value of BCIA is clear, but
   158	if an impact rarely propagates, then such a tool may be unnecessary. Therefore, we set out to understand how often BCIA detects
   159	propagation of an impact in real-world build maintenance activity.
   160	_Results:_ BuiScout detects impacts that propagate to unmodified
   161	parts of the build system in 77.37% of the 10 _,_ 000 studied change
   162	sets, suggesting that such a tool would regularly provide useful
   163	data to stakeholders.
   164	
   165	**RQ2. Impact Characteristics:** _**What are the characteristics of**_
   166	_**the propagating impact of build-modifying change sets?**_
   167	_Motivation:_ The impact of changes that we detect in RQ1 may vary
   168	in terms of their magnitude (i.e., the number of commands that
   169	are affected) and their breadth (i.e., the location of the affected
   170	commands with respect to the change set). Both characteristics can
   171	influence the applicability of BCIA. For example, even if changes
   172	regularly have an impact that propagates, if that impact is of a small
   173	magnitude or does not propagate broadly, practitioners may not
   174	need tool-support to assess the impact. Therefore, we set out to
   175	understand the magnitude and breadth of the impact that BCIA
   176	detects in real-world build maintenance activity.
   177	_Results:_ Change sets with a propagating impact affect an overall
   178	median of 14 commands and that only 4.45% of these commands
   179	are local to the files that the change set modified directly. The
   180	remaining 95.55% of impacted commands require practitioners to
   181	recognize how impact propagates across build specifications, which
   182	prior work suggests is a skill that many lack [12, 13].
