    35	
    36	This replication package is composed of the following:
    37	
    38	- The `Understanding_the_Implications_of_Changes_to_Build_Systems_Online_Appendix.pdf` file, the appendix to the paper containing further evaluations and discussions.
    39	
    40	- The `0_Data` directory contains all the data, including the intermediate results, used in the study. Detailed description of the content is provided in [Data](#data) section.
    41	
    42	- The `1_Data_Set_Curation` directory contains the scripts and data relating to the data set curation process. These include:
    43	    - The `1_WOC_includes_CMakeLists.txt.py`, `2_filter_and_collect_commits_and_ranking_metric.py`, `3_rank.py`, and `4_get_meta_data_and_latest_K_build_commits.py` scripts, which must be run sequentially.
    44	    - The `WOC_results_CMakeLists.txt.csv` file that substitutes for the output of the `1_WOC_includes_CMakeLists.txt.py` script to facilitate testing of the next steps.
    45	    - The `GitHub_tokens.txt` file in which at least one GitHub token must be listed for `2_filter_and_collect_commits_and_ranking_metric.py` script to run successfully.
    46	    - The `helpers.py` file, containing helper functions used by the `4_get_meta_data_and_latest_K_build_commits.py` script.
    47	    - The `ranking_metrics` directory, containing intermediate outputs for the artifact evaluation of the `2_filter_and_collect_commits_and_ranking_metric.py` script, which can be used in the following steps if the evaluator does not wish to use a GitHub token.
    48	    - The `collected_commits_per_project` directory, in which for each selected project `X = <project-owner>_<project-name>` that is analyzed in our study, a file `commits_X.csv` stores metadata of all of the commits in the project.
    49	    - The `ranked_candidate_projects.xlsx` file containing the ranked list of the candidate projects considered in the study, colour-coded to indicate our selection decision.
    50	    The [Data section](#data) describes the colour-codes.
    51	
    52	- The `2_BuiScout_v_ASE2024` directory contains BuiScout and the tools it relies on, in their version used to perform this study, and the data path required to test BuiScout.
    53	These include:
    54	    - The [`BuiScout`](https://github.com/mahtab-nejati/BuiScout/tree/ASE2024) directory, containing the ASE 2024 release of BuiScout's codebase.
    55	    - The [`gumtree`](https://github.com/mahtab-nejati/gumtree/tree/ASE2024) and [`tree-sitter-parser`](https://github.com/mahtab-nejati/tree-sitter-parser/tree/ASE2024) directories, each containing the revised versions of the tools that the ASE 2024 release of BuiScout depends on.
    56	    - The `_BuiScout_mountpoint` directory, where the input and output of BuiScout will be located. This directory contains:
    57	        - The `config.json` file, from which BuiScout reads configurations to analyze a sample commit from the [ET-Legacy](https://github.com/etlegacy/etlegacy) project.
    58	
